  "12A-p17-Q21b-1": {
   "steps": [
    {
     "text": "Velocity = derivative of position (Chain Rule).",
     "latex": "s\\prime(t)=\\dfrac{2t+8}{2\\sqrt{t^2+8t}}"
    },
    {
     "text": "At t = 2.",
     "latex": "s\\prime(2)=\\dfrac{12}{2\\sqrt{20}}=\\dfrac{6}{2\\sqrt5}=\\dfrac{3}{\\sqrt5}"
    },
    {
     "text": "Option C.",
     "latex": "\\frac{2 t + 8}{2 \\sqrt{t^{2} + 8 t}}"
    }
   ],
   "verified": true
  },
  "12A-p20-Q2-1": {
   "steps": [
    {
     "text": "A cubic with a local maximum and a local minimum has two turning points, where f′ = 0.",
     "latex": "f\\prime=0\\ \\text{twice}"
    },
    {
     "text": "The derivative of a cubic is a quadratic; f rises, falls, then rises, so f′ is +, −, +.",
     "latex": "+,\\ -,\\ +"
    },
    {
     "text": "So f′ is an upward-opening parabola with two distinct x-intercepts: option C.",
     "latex": "\\text{option C}"
    }
   ],
   "verified": true,
   "note": "read from the graph"
  },
  "12A-p28-Q10-1": {
   "steps": [
    {
     "text": "Power Rule works for any real exponent, including π.",
     "latex": "\\dfrac{d}{dt}t^{r}=rt^{r-1}"
